speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, in accordance with Standing Order 64(1), I wish to table the following Notices of Ways and Means Motions in both official languages:
(1)	To Amend the Statute Law Relating to Income Tax and to make related Amendments to the Canada Pension Plan and the Unemployment Insurance Act. 1971;
(2)	To Amend the Petroleum and Gas Revenue Tax Act;
(3)	To Amend the Excise Tax Act (1);
(4)	To Amend the Excise Tax Act (2);
(5)	To Amend the Excise Act;
(6)	To Amend the Customs Tariff;
(7)	To apply the customs and excise jurisdiction of Canada to the continental shelf of Canada and to amend certain Acts in relation thereto or in consequence thereof.
In accordance with Standing Order 64(2), I also ask you to designate the Order of the Day necessary for the consideration of each of these Ways and Means Motions.

Mr. Speaker, I move:
That when the House adjourns this day, it shall stand adjourned until two o'clock p.m., Thursday, December 8, 1983.
